    "payload": {
      "answer": "Four CLI commands over ONE job state machine: stop a job, wind a job back to an earlier point, continue a job, and restart a job from scratch. They are deliberately one piece of work rather than four, because they cannot be designed independently -- stop and restart must agree on what CANCELLED means before either can be written, and wind-back and continue must agree on what a restored point contains. Design the state machine first, then the four verbs fall out of it.",
